note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
note omegallm model.om (aien-train#52): geometry, forward pass and hand-derived backward pass
note (CONTRACT sections 1-3, CONTRACT-V1 section 1). Needs math.om and data.om before it.
note
note f64 values live in banked pools (one omc global holds at most 16777216 elements, and all
note globals together at most 2^30 bytes, omc error 23; CONTRACT-V3 section 2):
note  ow  parameter bank A: [0, SB) of the CONTRACT section 2 order, then a one-layer window of
note      LSTR values at og[36] and the final gain gf at og[37]; oww (lpool.om/epool.om) bank B holds
note      layers LA .. L-1 at (l - LA) LSTR. When P <= OWC, SB = GF, LA = L and ow is the v2 layout.
note      Every index outside the kernels is virtual (the section 2 order); owg/owp map it, and opx
note      maps a hot index of bank A or the staged layer (og[48]).
note  the gradient pool [0, 2P): GRD [0, P) in the platform cold store (ocsg/ocsp), BLK [P, 2P) in
note      ogr[j] below OGC and ogb[j - OGC] from OGC (j = i - P), reached through ogrg/ogrp/ogra
note  the Adam pool [0, 2P) (omvg/omvp): m at 0, v at P, at cold-store index P + i
note  oa  activations: layers below LAA at l ASTR, later layers in two windows at AW + (l mod 2) ASTR
note      flushed to bank B oab at (l - LAA) ASTR after their forward and staged back before their
note      backward; HF and the backward temporaries follow. When END <= OAC, LAA = L (v2 layout).
note  opa attention probabilities PA[l][n][t][j] of every layer
note og slots:
note  0 V  1 T  2 D  3 H  4 F  5 L  6 B  7 E=D/H  8 P  9 CT (positions in use, <= T)
note  10 GRD (base in the gradient pool of the gradient being accumulated: 0, or P for BLK) 11 MOM
note  (0 in the Adam pool) 12 VEL (P) 13 ACT (0 in oa) 14 ASTR (per-layer activation stride) 15 HF
note  16 SF 17 Z 18 PR 19 DH 20 DA 21 DQ 22 DK 23 DU 24 DO 25 DZ 26 DF 27 TMP 28 END
note  29 PSTR (per-layer PA stride H T T in opa) 30 WPE 31 LAY0 32 LSTR (per-layer parameter
note  stride) 33 GF 34 SB (first virtual index of bank B) 35 LA (first layer in bank B) 36 window base
note  in ow 37 gf in ow 38 LAA (first layer in the activation windows) 39 AW (activation window
note  base) 48 the layer staged in the parameter window (L: none)
note  40 seed S 41 step 42 TOTAL 43 lr bits 44 G (gradient blocks) 45 K (workers)
note  46 checkpoint magic of the run (1 OLLMCK01, 2 OLLMCK02, 3 OLLMCK03)
note  56 LV (layer applications) 57 LP 58 LC 59 NP (the loop, below) 60 set by a command that runs
note  looped checkpoints, before it loads one (ckpt.om refuses a looped one otherwise, exit 17)
note The loop (docs/LOOP.md): L stays the number of parameter layers. With NP > 1 the LC layers from
note layer LP (the core) are applied NP times in a row with the same weights, between the LP
note layers before them (the prelude) and the L - LP - LC after them (the coda), so a sequence
note passes LV = L + LC (NP - 1) layer applications. Application l runs parameter layer olp l.
note Activations, attention probabilities, the decode's row cache and the two activation banks are
note per application (oahin, opar, oaflip, okvkv take l); parameters and their gradients are per
note parameter layer (opg1 .. opw2 take the parameter layer, ovg1 .. ovw2 take l). Every gradient
note write adds, so a core weight's gradient is the sum over its NP applications. NP 0 or 1 is no
note loop: LV = L, olp l = l, and every result has the bits it had before the loop existed.
note Per layer activations (T rows of width D unless noted): HIN, A, Q, K, U, O, HMID, BN, S1[T],
note S2[T], FP[T][F] (pre-relu), RL[T][F]. Every sum runs over its index ascending.
note Sizes at the CONTRACT-V2 maxima (V 4096, T 256, D 384, H 16, F 1536, L 8), Wolfram:
note  P = V D + T D + L (4 D^2 + 2 D F + 2 D) + D -> 15833472
note  ASTR = 8 T D + 2 T + 2 T F -> 1573376; END = L ASTR + 10 T D + T + T V + T F + 4096 -> 15016192
note  and at the CONTRACT-V3 maxima (L 16): P 29995392, PA = L H T T -> 16777216; the bank-B sizes
note  are in lpool.om. ogeom refuses any layout past a pool.
note Bank A capacities: OWC parameters, OGC BLK values, OAC activations (the bank-crossing test
note build of tests/omegallm/build.sh shrinks all three).
const OWC ulong 15833472
global ow f64 15833472
const OGC ulong 15833472
global ogr f64 15833472
const OAC ulong 16777216
global oa f64 16777216
const OPAN ulong 16777216
global opa f64 16777216

note Neuralese Phase 1: non-destructive steering, adaptive looped-core thought, LTP0 latent handoff & live telemetry.
note All disabled when onlc[0]=0, onlc[4]=0, onlc[6]=0, onlc[10]=0 -> bit-identical to stock ollm.
note onlc: [0]=steer_on, [1]=steer_layer (999=all), [2]=steer_kind (1=neuron scale, 2=resid bias, 3=head scale),
note       [3]=steer_idx, [4]=adapt_extra (0..4), [5]=adapt_thresh_milli (nats*1000),
note       [6]=ltp_inject_on, [7]=ltp_inject_layer, [8]=last_extra_loops, [9]=last_lv_used, [10]=trace_on
global onlc ulong 16
note onlf: [0]=steer_val, [1]=ltp_alpha, [2]=last_entropy, [3]=last_surprisal, [4]=last_max_prob, [5]=last_hf_norm
global onlf f64 8
global onlv f64 384
global onlh f64 384
global onln f64 32
global onla f64 16
global onltn_i ulong 16
global onltn_v f64 16

note gradient pool element i (i < 2 P)
fn ogrg i ulong to f64
p = get og 8
if lt i p
ret ocsg i
end
j = sub i p
if lt j OGC
ret get ogr j
end
ret get ogb sub j OGC
end

fn ogrp i ulong v f64 to void
p = get og 8
if lt i p
ocsp i v
ret
end
j = sub i p
if lt j OGC
put ogr j v
else
put ogb sub j OGC v
end
end

note gradient pool element i += a
fn ogra i ulong a f64 to void
p = get og 8
if lt i p
ocsp i add ocsg i a
ret
end
j = sub i p
if lt j OGC
put ogr j add get ogr j a
else
k = sub j OGC
put ogb k add get ogb k a
end
end

note Adam pool element i (i < 2 P), cold-store index P + i
fn omvg i ulong to f64
ret ocsg add get og 8 i
end

fn omvp i ulong v f64 to void
ocsp add get og 8 i v
end

note parameter at virtual index i (bank A, bank B or gf), and its store
fn owg i ulong to f64
sb = get og 34
if lt i sb
ret get ow i
end
g = get og 33
if ge i g
ret get ow add get og 37 sub i g
end
ret get oww sub i sb
end

fn owp i ulong v f64 to void
sb = get og 34
if lt i sb
put ow i v
ret
end
g = get og 33
if ge i g
put ow add get og 37 sub i g v
ret
end
put oww sub i sb v
end

note ow index of virtual index i for the kernels: bank A as is, gf at og[37], a bank-B layer only
note when it is the staged layer og[48] (else exit 16, a missing ostw)
fn opx i ulong to ulong
if lt i get og 34
ret i
end
g = get og 33
if ge i g
ret add get og 37 sub i g
end
l = div sub i get og 31 get og 32
if ne l get og 48
exit 16
end
ret add get og 36 sub i opg1 l
end

note Mutant y (wrong bank-B layer: ostw stages layer LA's block for every layer): 1 in the product,
note 0 in the mutant.
const OMUTY ulong 1

const OCH ulong 999999

note stage bank-B layer l into the parameter window (layers below LA live in bank A)
fn ostw l ulong to void
la = get og 35
if lt l la
ret
end
n = get og 32
s = mul sub l la n
if eq OMUTY 0
s = 0
end
ostwc get og 36 s n
put og 48 l
end

note ow[wb + i] = oww[s + i] for i < n (chunked: a loop runs at most 999999 passes)
fn ostwc wb ulong s ulong n ulong to void
for q ulong ocn n
i = mul q OCH
ie = oce q n
while lt i ie bound 999999
put ow add wb i get oww add s i
i = add i 1
end
end
end

note copy layer l's activation block between its window and bank B oab (to oab when fo)
fn oaflip l ulong fo bool to void
la = get og 38
if lt l la
ret
end
n = get og 14
s = mul sub l la n
oaflc oahin l s n fo
end

note oab[s + i] = oa[w + i] for i < n when fo, else the reverse
fn oaflc w ulong s ulong n ulong fo bool to void
if fo
oafo w s n
else
oafi w s n
end
end

fn oafo w ulong s ulong n ulong to void
for q ulong ocn n
i = mul q OCH
ie = oce q n
while lt i ie bound 999999
put oab add s i get oa add w i
i = add i 1
end
end
end

fn oafi w ulong s ulong n ulong to void
for q ulong ocn n
i = mul q OCH
ie = oce q n
while lt i ie bound 999999
put oa add w i get oab add s i
i = add i 1
end
end
end

note TMP holds V logits (sample) or T attention dots
const OTMP ulong 4096

note Mutant a (attention backward sign flip in the dK term): 1 in the product, 0 in the mutant.
const OMUTA ulong 1

note Configure og from og[0..6]; false when a shape is zero, over the maximum, or D mod H != 0, or
note when the layout does not fit the pools.
fn ogeom to bool
if not ogok
ret false
end
t = get og 1
d = get og 2
put og 7 div d get og 3
u = mul 4 mul d d
u = add u mul 2 mul d get og 4
u = add u mul 2 d
put og 32 u
put og 30 mul get og 0 d
u = mul t d
put og 31 add get og 30 u
u = mul get og 5 get og 32
put og 33 add get og 31 u
u = add get og 33 d
put og 8 u
put og 9 t
put og 10 0
put og 11 0
put og 12 u
put og 13 0
put og 29 mul mul get og 3 t t
if not oglv
ret false
end
u = mul t d
put og 14 oastr u
if not ogwb
ret false
end
if not ogab u
ret false
end
p = get og 8
if gt p add OGC OGBN
ret false
end
if gt mul 3 p ocsinit
ret false
end
ret le mul get og 56 get og 29 OPAN
end

note the layer applications og[56] from L and the loop og[57 .. 59]; false when the core is empty,
note does not fit in the L layers, or runs more passes than the attention pool has rows for
fn oglv to bool
ll = get og 5
np = get og 59
if le np 1
put og 56 ll
ret true
end
lc = get og 58
if or eq lc 0 gt np OPAN
ret false
end
if gt add get og 57 lc ll
ret false
end
put og 56 add ll mul lc sub np 1
ret true
end

note the parameter layer that layer application l runs
fn olp l ulong to ulong
np = get og 59
if le np 1
ret l
end
lp = get og 57
if lt l lp
ret l
end
lc = get og 58
j = sub l lp
if lt j mul lc np
ret add lp rem j lc
end
ret sub l mul lc sub np 1
end

note parameter banks: v2 layout when P <= OWC, else LA layers in bank A, the window and gf after
note them, layers LA .. L-1 in oww
fn ogwb to bool
ll = get og 5
g = get og 33
put og 34 g
put og 35 ll
put og 36 g
put og 37 g
put og 48 ll
if le get og 8 OWC
ret true
end
ls = get og 32
nd = add add get og 31 ls get og 2
if lt OWC nd
ret false
end
la = div sub OWC nd ls
if gt mul sub ll la ls OWWN
ret false
end
sb = add get og 31 mul la ls
put og 34 sb
put og 35 la
put og 36 sb
put og 37 add sb ls
ret true
end

note activation banks: v2 layout when END <= OAC, else LAA layers, two windows, then HF and the
note backward temporaries
fn ogab td ulong to bool
ll = get og 56
st = get og 14
put og 38 ll
put og 39 mul ll st
ogeom3 td mul ll st
ogeom2 td
if le get og 28 OAC
ret true
end
w2 = add sub get og 28 get og 15 mul 2 st
if lt OAC w2
ret false
end
la = div sub OAC w2 st
if gt mul sub ll la st OABN
ret false
end
aw = mul la st
put og 38 la
put og 39 aw
ogeom3 td add aw mul 2 st
ogeom2 td
ret le get og 28 OAC
end

fn ogeom3 td ulong hf ulong to void
put og 15 hf
put og 16 add get og 15 td
put og 17 add get og 16 get og 1
put og 18 add get og 17 td
end

note per-layer activation stride: 8 T D + 2 T + 2 T F
fn oastr td ulong to ulong
t = get og 1
a = add mul 8 td mul 2 t
ret add a mul mul 2 t get og 4
end

note shape limits (CONTRACT-V3 section 1): every shape >= 1, 256 <= V <= 4096, T <= 256,
note D <= 384, H <= 16, F <= 1536, L <= 16, B <= 64, D mod H = 0
fn ogok to bool
for i ulong 7
if eq get og i 0
ret false
end
end
if or lt get og 0 256 gt get og 0 4096
ret false
end
if or gt get og 1 256 gt get og 2 384
ret false
end
if or gt get og 3 16 gt get og 4 1536
ret false
end
if or gt get og 5 16 gt get og 6 64
ret false
end
ret eq rem get og 2 get og 3 0
end

fn ogeom2 td ulong to void
t = get og 1
put og 19 add get og 18 mul t get og 0
put og 20 add get og 19 td
put og 21 add get og 20 td
put og 22 add get og 21 td
put og 23 add get og 22 td
put og 24 add get og 23 td
put og 25 add get og 24 td
put og 26 add get og 25 td
put og 27 add get og 26 mul t get og 4
put og 28 add get og 27 OTMP
end

note parameter offsets of layer l
fn opg1 l ulong to ulong
ret add get og 31 mul l get og 32
end
fn opwq l ulong to ulong
ret add opg1 l get og 2
end
fn opwk l ulong to ulong
d = get og 2
ret add opwq l mul d d
end
fn opwv l ulong to ulong
d = get og 2
ret add opwk l mul d d
end
fn opwo l ulong to ulong
d = get og 2
ret add opwv l mul d d
end
fn opg2 l ulong to ulong
d = get og 2
ret add opwo l mul d d
end
fn opw1 l ulong to ulong
ret add opg2 l get og 2
end
fn opw2 l ulong to ulong
ret add opw1 l mul get og 2 get og 4
end

note parameter offsets of layer application l
fn ovg1 l ulong to ulong
ret opg1 olp l
end
fn ovwq l ulong to ulong
ret opwq olp l
end
fn ovwk l ulong to ulong
ret opwk olp l
end
fn ovwv l ulong to ulong
ret opwv olp l
end
fn ovwo l ulong to ulong
ret opwo olp l
end
fn ovg2 l ulong to ulong
ret opg2 olp l
end
fn ovw1 l ulong to ulong
ret opw1 olp l
end
fn ovw2 l ulong to ulong
ret opw2 olp l
end

note activation offsets of layer l (layers from LAA in the two windows at AW)
fn oahin l ulong to ulong
if lt l get og 38
ret add get og 13 mul l get og 14
end
ret add get og 39 mul rem l 2 get og 14
end
fn oatd n ulong to ulong
ret mul n mul get og 1 get og 2
end
fn oaa l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 1
end
fn oaq l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 2
end
fn oak l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 3
end
fn oau l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 4
end
fn oao l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 5
end
fn oahm l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 6
end
fn oabn l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 7
end
fn oas1 l ulong to ulong
ret add oahin l oatd 8
end
fn oas2 l ulong to ulong
ret add oas1 l get og 1
end
fn oafp l ulong to ulong
ret add oas2 l get og 1
end
fn oarl l ulong to ulong
ret add oafp l mul get og 1 get og 4
end
note output rows of layer application l: the next one's HIN, or HF after the last
fn oaout l ulong to ulong
if lt add l 1 get og 56
ret oahin add l 1
end
ret get og 15
end

note Kernels. The fast forms keep every v0 sum: each output is one accumulator that starts at
note 0.0 and adds its terms in the v0 index order with the v0 expression (add s mul a w); four
note outputs run side by side in separate accumulators, so every result has v0's bits. Results of
note the four-wide blocks pass through oq.
global oq f64 4

note y[0..c) = x[0..r) . W[r][c] (overwrites y); x, y in oa, W in ow at virtual index wv
fn kvm xo ulong wv ulong yo ulong r ulong c ulong to void
wo = opx wv
xe = add xo r
j = ulong 0
while le add j 4 c bound 999999
kvmb xo xe add wo j c
kput4 add yo j
j = add j 4
end
while lt j c bound 4
put oa add yo j kvm1 xo xe add wo j c
j = add j 1
end
end

note oa[yo..yo+4) = oq[0..4)
fn kput4 yo ulong to void
put oa yo get oq 0
put oa add yo 1 get oq 1
put oa add yo 2 get oq 2
put oa add yo 3 get oq 3
end

note oq[m] = sum over xo <= i < xe of x[i] W[wi + m + (i - xo) c], m < 4
fn kvmb xo ulong xe ulong wi ulong c ulong to void
s0 = 0.0f64
s1 = 0.0f64
s2 = 0.0f64
s3 = 0.0f64
while lt xo xe bound 999999
a = get oa xo
s0 = add s0 mul a get ow wi
s1 = add s1 mul a get ow add wi 1
s2 = add s2 mul a get ow add wi 2
s3 = add s3 mul a get ow add wi 3
wi = add wi c
xo = add xo 1
end
put oq 0 s0
put oq 1 s1
put oq 2 s2
put oq 3 s3
end

note sum over xo <= i < xe of x[i] W[wi + (i - xo) c]
fn kvm1 xo ulong xe ulong wi ulong c ulong to f64
s = 0.0f64
while lt xo xe bound 999999
a = get oa xo
s = add s mul a get ow wi
wi = add wi c
xo = add xo 1
end
ret s
end

note y[k] += sum_j dy[j] W[k][j] for k < r, j < c (y += dy . W^T); dy, y in oa, W in ow at virtual
note index wv
fn kvta dyo ulong wv ulong yo ulong r ulong c ulong to void
wo = opx wv
de = add dyo c
k = ulong 0
while le add k 4 r bound 999999
kdot4 dyo de add wo mul k c c
kacc4 add yo k
k = add k 4
end
while lt k r bound 4
a = add get oa add yo k kdot1 dyo de add wo mul k c
put oa add yo k a
k = add k 1
end
end

note oa[yo + m] = oa[yo + m] + oq[m], m < 4
fn kacc4 yo ulong to void
put oa yo add get oa yo get oq 0
q = add yo 1
put oa q add get oa q get oq 1
q = add yo 2
put oa q add get oa q get oq 2
q = add yo 3
put oa q add get oa q get oq 3
end

note oq[m] = sum over xo <= i < xe of x[i] W[wi + m c + (i - xo)], m < 4; x in oa, W in ow
fn kdot4 xo ulong xe ulong wi ulong c ulong to void
s0 = 0.0f64
s1 = 0.0f64
s2 = 0.0f64
s3 = 0.0f64
w2 = add wi add c c
while lt xo xe bound 999999
a = get oa xo
s0 = add s0 mul a get ow wi
s1 = add s1 mul a get ow add wi c
s2 = add s2 mul a get ow w2
s3 = add s3 mul a get ow add w2 c
wi = add wi 1
w2 = add w2 1
xo = add xo 1
end
put oq 0 s0
put oq 1 s1
put oq 2 s2
put oq 3 s3
end

note sum over xo <= i < xe of x[i] W[wi + (i - xo)]; x in oa, W in ow
fn kdot1 xo ulong xe ulong wi ulong to f64
s = 0.0f64
while lt xo xe bound 999999
a = get oa xo
s = add s mul a get ow wi
wi = add wi 1
xo = add xo 1
end
ret s
end

note kdot4 with both operands in oa
fn kdot4a xo ulong xe ulong wi ulong c ulong to void
s0 = 0.0f64
s1 = 0.0f64
s2 = 0.0f64
s3 = 0.0f64
w2 = add wi add c c
while lt xo xe bound 999999
a = get oa xo
s0 = add s0 mul a get oa wi
s1 = add s1 mul a get oa add wi c
s2 = add s2 mul a get oa w2
s3 = add s3 mul a get oa add w2 c
wi = add wi 1
w2 = add w2 1
xo = add xo 1
end
put oq 0 s0
put oq 1 s1
put oq 2 s2
put oq 3 s3
end

note kdot1 with both operands in oa
fn kdot1a xo ulong xe ulong wi ulong to f64
s = 0.0f64
while lt xo xe bound 999999
a = get oa xo
s = add s mul a get oa wi
wi = add wi 1
xo = add xo 1
end
ret s
end

note G[k][j] += x[k] dy[j] for k < r, j < c (outer product into a gradient); x, dy in oa, G in ogr
fn kger xo ulong dyo ulong go ulong r ulong c ulong to void
for k ulong r
kger1 get oa add xo k add go mul k c dyo c
end
end

note G[gi + j] += xv dy[j] for j < c (elements independent, four per pass)
fn kger1 xv f64 gi ulong yi ulong c ulong to void
ye = add yi c
while le add yi 4 ye bound 999999
ogra gi mul xv get oa yi
ogra add gi 1 mul xv get oa add yi 1
ogra add gi 2 mul xv get oa add yi 2
ogra add gi 3 mul xv get oa add yi 3
gi = add gi 4
yi = add yi 4
end
while lt yi ye bound 4
ogra gi mul xv get oa yi
gi = add gi 1
yi = add yi 1
end
end

note y[i] += a x[i]; x, y in oa
fn kaxpy yo ulong xo ulong a f64 n ulong to void
for i ulong n
q = add yo i
v = mul a get oa add xo i
put oa q add get oa q v
end
end

note y[i] += a x[i]; x in oa, y in the gradient pool
fn kaxpg yo ulong xo ulong a f64 n ulong to void
for i ulong n
ogra add yo i mul a get oa add xo i
end
end

fn ozero o ulong n ulong to void
for i ulong n
put oa add o i 0.0f64
end
end

fn ozerog o ulong n ulong to void
for q ulong ocn n
i = mul q OCH
ie = oce q n
while lt i ie bound 999999
ogrp add o i 0.0f64
i = add i 1
end
end
end

note A loop runs at most 999999 passes (the while bound; a for over a name has the same guard), so
note loops over P or more run in ocn n chunks of OCH; chunk q covers [q OCH, oce q n).
fn ocn n ulong to ulong
ret div add n 999998 OCH
end
fn oce q ulong n ulong to ulong
e = mul add q 1 OCH
if gt e n
ret n
end
ret e
end

note y = rms(v, g): s = sqrt((sum v^2)/D + 1e-5) stored at so; y[i] = (v[i]/s) g[i]; g at virtual
note index gv
fn frms vo ulong gv ulong yo ulong so ulong to void
go = opx gv
d = get og 2
ss = 0.0f64
for i ulong d
v = get oa add vo i
ss = add ss mul v v
end
s = fsqrt add div ss f64 d 0.00001
put oa so s
for j ulong d
v = div get oa add vo j s
v = mul v get ow add go j
put oa add yo j v
end
end

note rms backward: n = v/s, dn = da g, c = (sum dn n)/D; dv = (dn - n c)/s added to dh;
note dg += da n added to the gain's gradient. go is the gain's virtual index.
global ofs f64 8
fn brms vo ulong go ulong so ulong dao ulong dho ulong to void
d = get og 2
put ofs 0 get oa so
gg = add get og 10 go
go = opx go
put ofs 1 div brmsc vo go dao get ofs 0 f64 d
for j ulong d
brms1 add vo j add go j add dao j add dho j add gg j
end
end

note sum over i < D of (da[i] g[i]) (v[i]/s), ascending
fn brmsc vo ulong go ulong dao ulong s f64 to f64
c = 0.0f64
for i ulong get og 2
dn = get oa add dao i
dn = mul dn get ow add go i
v = div get oa add vo i s
c = add c mul dn v
end
ret c
end

note one element of the rms backward; s = ofs[0], c = ofs[1]
fn brms1 vp ulong gp ulong dap ulong dhp ulong ggp ulong to void
s = get ofs 0
n = div get oa vp s
da = get oa dap
ogra ggp mul da n
dn = mul da get ow gp
dn = div sub dn mul n get ofs 1 s
put oa dhp add get oa dhp dn
end

note z[i] = a[i] + b[i] for i < n (all in oa)
fn kadd3 zo ulong ao ulong bo ulong n ulong to void
for i ulong n
v = get oa add ao i
v = add v get oa add bo i
put oa add zo i v
end
end

note z[i] = a[i] + b[i] for i < n (a, b in ow, z in oa)
fn kadd3w zo ulong ao ulong bo ulong n ulong to void
for i ulong n
v = get ow add ao i
v = add v get ow add bo i
put oa add zo i v
end
end

note h[t] = wte[x[t]] + wpe[t] for sequence b of the batch
fn oemb b ulong to void
d = get og 2
tt = get og 1
for t ulong get og 9
wr = get obx add mul b tt t
wr = mul wr d
pr = add get og 30 mul t d
kadd3w add oahin 0 mul t d wr pr d
end
end

note offset in opa of PA[n][t][0] of layer l
fn opar l ulong n ulong t ulong to ulong
tt = get og 1
p = add mul n tt t
ret add mul l get og 29 mul p tt
end

note attention scores and softmax of head n, row t: PA[n][t][j] for j <= t
fn fatts l ulong n ulong t ulong to void
e = get og 7
qo = add add oaq l mul t get og 2 mul n e
ko = add oak l mul n e
pa = opar l n t
m = fattsk qo ko pa add t 1
sm = osofp pa add t 1 m
end

note PA row: s[j] = q.k[j]/sqrt(E) for j < nj, k rows stepping by D; returns the max score
fn fattsk qo ulong ko ulong pa ulong nj ulong to f64
d = get og 2
e = get og 7
isq = fsqrt f64 e
m = bitcast f64 ulong 18442240474082181120
qe = add qo e
j = ulong 0
while le add j 4 nj bound 999999
kdot4a qo qe ko d
m = fattp4 add pa j isq m
ko = add ko mul 4 d
j = add j 4
end
while lt j nj bound 4
s = div kdot1a qo qe ko isq
put opa add pa j s
m = fmax m s
ko = add ko d
j = add j 1
end
ret m
end

note PA[p + m] = oq[m] / isq for m < 4 in order; returns the running max
fn fattp4 p ulong isq f64 m f64 to f64
for i ulong 4
s = div get oq i isq
put opa add p i s
m = fmax m s
end
ret m
end

note p = exp(x - m) / sum over n entries at o in oa (in place); returns sum
fn osoft o ulong n ulong m f64 to f64
sm = 0.0f64
for j ulong n
ev = fexp sub get oa add o j m
put oa add o j ev
sm = add sm ev
end
for k ulong n
v = div get oa add o k sm
put oa add o k v
end
ret sm
end

note osoft on opa
fn osofp o ulong n ulong m f64 to f64
sm = 0.0f64
for j ulong n
ev = fexp sub get opa add o j m
put opa add o j ev
sm = add sm ev
end
for k ulong n
v = div get opa add o k sm
put opa add o k v
end
ret sm
end

note o[t][nE + i] = sum_{j <= t} p[t][j] u[j][nE + i]
fn fatto l ulong n ulong t ulong to void
e = get og 7
oo = add add oao l mul t get og 2 mul n e
uo = add oau l mul n e
pa = opar l n t
ozero oo e
fattok oo uo pa add t 1
end

note o[0..E) += p[j] u[j][0..E) for j < nj, u rows stepping by D
fn fattok oo ulong uo ulong pa ulong nj ulong to void
d = get og 2
e = get og 7
for j ulong nj
kaxpy oo uo get opa add pa j e
uo = add uo d
end
end

fn olayf l ulong to void
ostw olp l
for t ulong get og 9
olayf1 l t
end
for n ulong get og 3
for t2 ulong get og 9
fatts l n t2
fatto l n t2
end
end
for t3 ulong get og 9
olayf2 l t3
end
oaflip l true
end

note row t: a = rms(h, g1); q, k, u = a.wq, a.wk, a.wv
fn olayf1 l ulong t ulong to void
d = get og 2
r = mul t d
a = add oaa l r
frms add oahin l r ovg1 l a add oas1 l t
kvm a ovwq l add oaq l r d d
kvm a ovwk l add oak l r d d
kvm a ovwv l add oau l r d d
end

note row t: h += o.wo; b = rms(h, g2); out = h + relu(b.w1).w2
fn olayf2 l ulong t ulong to void
d = get og 2
f = get og 4
r = mul t d
hm = add oahm l r
kvm add oao l r ovwo l hm d d
kadd3 hm add oahin l r hm d
frms hm ovg2 l add oabn l r add oas2 l t
fp = add oafp l mul t f
kvm add oabn l r ovw1 l fp d f
rl = add oarl l mul t f
krelu rl fp f
if ne get onlc 0 0
onlsteer_ffn l t
end
ou = add oaout l r
kvm rl ovw2 l ou f d
kadd3 ou hm ou d
if ne get onlc 0 0
onlsteer_res l t
end
end

note y[j] = x[j] when x[j] > 0, else 0, for j < n
fn krelu yo ulong xo ulong n ulong to void
for j ulong n
v = get oa add xo j
if le v 0.0
v = 0.0f64
end
put oa add yo j v
end
end

note loss of row t: the logits at o (n entries) become probabilities; returns
note log(sum exp(l - max)) - (l_y - max)
fn olossrow o ulong n ulong y ulong to f64
m = bitcast f64 ulong 18442240474082181120
for j ulong n
m = fmax m get oa add o j
end
ly = get oa add o y
sm = osoft o n m
ret sub flog sm sub ly m
end

note final rms, tied head and loss of sequence b; returns the mean loss over CT positions
fn ohead b ulong to f64
ls = 0.0f64
for t ulong get og 9
ls = add ls oheadr b t
end
ret div ls f64 get og 9
end

note row t of the head: z = rms(HF[t], gf); logits = z . wte^T; returns the row loss
fn oheadr b ulong t ulong to f64
d = get og 2
r = mul t d
z = add get og 17 r
hf = add get og 15 r
frms hf get og 33 z add get og 16 t
pr = add get og 18 mul t get og 0
klogit z pr get og 0 d
y = get oby add mul b get og 1 t
ret olossrow pr get og 0 y
end

note p[c] = z . wte[c] for c < n (wte rows of length d at offset 0 of ow; z, p in oa)
fn klogit zo ulong po ulong n ulong d ulong to void
ze = add zo d
c = ulong 0
while le add c 4 n bound 999999
kdot4 zo ze mul c d d
kput4 add po c
c = add c 4
end
while lt c n bound 4
put oa add po c kdot1 zo ze mul c d
c = add c 1
end
end

note ogkm[0] = 0: the backward ReLU mask is the sign of this pass's own FP (every command but
note gcmp2); 1: offb calls ogmask, which gpu/gg.om defines for gcmp2 (the chip's FP sign) and
note nogpu.om defines as a refusal on the CPU-only targets. ogkm[1] = the sequence in flight.
global ogkm ulong 2
note ofzlay: when > 0, obwd stops after layer ofzlay[0] and skips obwde (frozen base layers).
global ofzlay ulong 1

note okv (ham/ollm-speed): the CPU decode's row reuse. okv[0] = the rows of obx row 0 whose layer
note activations the last ofwdi left valid, okvt[0..okv[0]) their tokens. ofwd clears okv[0]: it
note rewrites the same activation rows for any sequence b.
global okv ulong 1
global okvt ulong 16384
note OMUTI: 1 in the product; 0 in mutant i (okvlcp trusts okv[0] without comparing the tokens), which
note kvcmp must catch.
const OMUTI ulong 1

note forward pass of sequence b (x in obx, y in oby); returns its mean loss
fn ofwd b ulong to f64
put okv 0 0
put ogkm 1 b
oemb b
for l ulong get og 56
olayf l
end
ret ohead b
end

note the first row ofwdi computes: the common prefix of obx row 0 and okvt, at most okv[0] and
note CT - 1 (the last row is always recomputed). Bank-B layers (l >= LAA) restore/save only their
note K/V slices (oak/oau) in oab without touching oahin, so KV cache works identically for all L.
fn okvlcp to ulong
ct = get og 9
n = get okv 0
if ge n ct
n = sub ct 1
end
if eq OMUTI 0
ret n
end
for i ulong n
if ne get obx i get okvt i
ret i
end
end
ret n
end

note ofwdi: ofwd 0 for the decode (olastf on the CPU): rows t0..CT-1 of every layer, t0 = okvlcp,
note then the final RMS of row CT - 1 only (olast's z; no head for the other rows, no loss). A causal
note row reads only rows at or before it, rows below t0 hold what the same model.om row functions
note computed for the same tokens at the same positions, so olast's logits are bit-identical to
note ofwd 0 then olast (kvcmp checks every step). Returns t0.
fn ofwdi to ulong
t0 = okvlcp
put okv 0 0
put ogkm 1 0
ct = get og 9
nr = sub ct t0
okvemb t0 nr
for l ulong get og 56
okvlay l t0 nr
end
okvend ct
ret t0
end

note oemb for rows t0 .. t0 + nr - 1 of sequence 0
fn okvemb t0 ulong nr ulong to void
d = get og 2
for i ulong nr
t = add t0 i
wr = mul get obx t d
pr = add get og 30 mul t d
kadd3w add oahin 0 mul t d wr pr d
end
end

note Bank-B KV slice transfer for layer l >= LAA: copy rows [r0 .. r0 + cnt) of oak and oau
note between oa and oab (to oab when fo, else from oab). Never touches oahin.
fn okvkv l ulong r0 ulong cnt ulong fo bool to void
la = get og 38
if or lt l la eq cnt 0
ret
end
d = get og 2
off = mul r0 d
n = mul cnt d
s = mul sub l la get og 14
oaflc add oak l off add add s oatd 3 off n fo
oaflc add oau l off add add s oatd 4 off n fo
end

note olayf l for rows t0 .. t0 + nr - 1
fn okvlay l ulong t0 ulong nr ulong to void
ostw olp l
okvkv l 0 t0 false
if ne get onlc 6 0
for i0 ulong nr
onlinject l add t0 i0
end
end
for i ulong nr
olayf1 l add t0 i
end
for n ulong get og 3
for i2 ulong nr
t = add t0 i2
fatts l n t
fatto l n t
end
end
if ne get onlc 0 0
for ih ulong nr
onlsteer_head l add t0 ih
end
end
for i3 ulong nr
olayf2 l add t0 i3
end
okvkv l t0 nr true
if ne get onlc 10 0
onlrec_lay l sub add t0 nr 1
end
end

note the final RMS of row CT - 1 into z (olast reads it), then okv = the CT context tokens
fn okvend ct ulong to void
d = get og 2
t = sub ct 1
r = mul t d
hf = add get og 15 r
z = add get og 17 r
frms hf get og 33 z add get og 16 t
for i ulong ct
put okvt i get obx i
end
put okv 0 ct
if ne get onlc 10 0
onlrec_top t
end
end

note ======== Neuralese Phase 1 helpers (non-destructive steering, LTP0 injection, telemetry, adaptive looping)

fn onlreset to void
for i ulong 16
put onlc i 0
end
for j ulong 8
put onlf j 0.0f64
end
end

fn onlmatchl l ulong to bool
tl = get onlc 1
ret or eq tl 999 eq tl l
end

fn onlsteer_head l ulong t ulong to void
if or ne get onlc 2 3 not onlmatchl l
ret
end
hi = get onlc 3
if ge hi get og 3
ret
end
e = get og 7
oo = add add oao l mul t get og 2 mul hi e
sc = get onlf 0
for i ulong e
q = add oo i
put oa q mul get oa q sc
end
end

fn onlsteer_ffn l ulong t ulong to void
if or ne get onlc 2 1 not onlmatchl l
ret
end
idx = get onlc 3
f = get og 4
if ge idx f
ret
end
q = add add oarl l mul t f idx
put oa q mul get oa q get onlf 0
end

fn onlsteer_res l ulong t ulong to void
if or ne get onlc 2 2 not onlmatchl l
ret
end
idx = get onlc 3
d = get og 2
if ge idx d
ret
end
q = add add oaout l mul t d idx
put oa q add get oa q get onlf 0
end

fn onlv_rms d ulong to f64
ss = 0.0f64
for i ulong d
v = get onlv i
ss = add ss mul v v
end
ret fsqrt add div ss f64 d 1.0e-12f64
end

fn onlinject l ulong t ulong to void
if ne l get onlc 7
ret
end
d = get og 2
ho = add oahin l mul t d
sc = div get onlf 1 onlv_rms d
for i ulong d
q = add ho i
dv = mul sc get onlv i
put oa q add get oa q dv
end
end

fn onlrec_lay l ulong t ulong to void
if ge l 32
ret
end
d = get og 2
ou = add oaout l mul t d
ss = 0.0f64
for i ulong d
v = get oa add ou i
ss = add ss mul v v
end
put onln l fsqrt ss
end

fn onlrec_hf t ulong to void
d = get og 2
hf = add get og 15 mul t d
ss = 0.0f64
for i ulong d
v = get oa add hf i
put onlh i v
ss = add ss mul v v
end
put onlf 5 fsqrt ss
end

fn onlrec_att ll ulong t ulong to void
h = get og 3
for n ulong h
pa = opar ll n t
mx = 0.0f64
for j ulong add t 1
pv = get opa add pa j
if gt pv mx
mx = pv
end
end
put onla n mx
end
end

fn onlrec_top t ulong to void
onlrec_hf t
ll = sub get og 56 1
onlrec_att ll t
onlrec_neur ll t
end

fn onlrec_neur ll ulong t ulong to void
f = get og 4
rl = add oarl ll mul t f
for k ulong 16
put onltn_i k 0
put onltn_v k -1.0f64
end
for j ulong f
v = get oa add rl j
if gt v get onltn_v 15
onlins_neur j v
end
end
end

fn onlins_neur idx ulong val f64 to void
pos = ulong 15
while gt pos 0 bound 16
pv = get onltn_v sub pos 1
if le val pv
break
end
put onltn_i pos get onltn_i sub pos 1
put onltn_v pos pv
pos = sub pos 1
end
put onltn_i pos idx
put onltn_v pos val
end

fn onlent_max o ulong v ulong to f64
m = bitcast f64 ulong 18442240474082181120
for c ulong v
x = get oa add o c
if gt x m
m = x
end
end
ret m
end

fn onlent_lsm o ulong v ulong m f64 to f64
sm = 0.0f64
for c ulong v
sm = add sm fexp sub get oa add o c m
end
ret flog sm
end

note Non-destructive Shannon entropy (nats) and max-prob of current TMP[0..V) logits
fn onlentropy to f64
o = get og 27
v = get og 0
m = onlent_max o v
lsm = onlent_lsm o v m
ent = 0.0f64
mxp = 0.0f64
for c ulong v
lp = sub sub get oa add o c m lsm
p = fexp lp
if gt p mxp
mxp = p
end
if gt p 1.0e-15f64
ent = sub ent mul p lp
end
end
put onlf 2 ent
put onlf 4 mxp
ret ent
end

fn onlcopy_oa dst ulong src ulong d ulong to void
for i ulong d
put oa add dst i get oa add src i
end
end

note Single extra continuous-thought pass through core layers [c0 .. c0+cn) from pre-coda core output, then coda on row t
fn onlpass1 t ulong c0 ulong cn ulong to void
d = get og 2
r = mul t d
coda = sub get og 5 add c0 cn
lv = get og 56
if gt coda 0
csrc = add oaout sub sub lv coda 1 r
onlcopy_oa add oahin c0 r csrc d
else
onlcopy_oa add oahin c0 r add get og 15 r d
end
for k ulong cn
okvlay add c0 k t 1
end
src = add oaout sub add c0 cn 1 r
if gt coda 0
cstart = sub lv coda
onlcopy_oa add oahin cstart r src d
for k2 ulong coda
okvlay add cstart k2 t 1
end
else
onlcopy_oa add get og 15 r src d
end
end

note Entropy-gated adaptive continuous-thought looping after olastf (when onlc[4] > 0)
fn onladapt to void
put onlc 8 0
put onlc 9 get og 56
ent = onlentropy
ex = get onlc 4
if eq ex 0
ret
end
if gt ex 4
ex = 4
end
th = div f64 get onlc 5 1000.0
if and gt get onlc 5 0 lt ent th
ret
end
onladapt_run ex th
end

fn onladapt_run ex ulong th f64 to void
ct = get og 9
t = sub ct 1
c0 = get og 57
cn = get og 58
if eq cn 0
c0 = sub get og 5 1
cn = 1
end
for ps ulong ex
onlpass1 t c0 cn
okvend ct
olast
ent = onlentropy
put onlc 8 add ps 1
put onlc 9 add get onlc 9 cn
if and gt get onlc 5 0 lt ent th
break
end
end
end

note backward of the head for row t: dl = (p - onehot(y)) sc; dwte += dl z; dz = dl . wte;
note DH[t] = rms backward of HF[t].
fn ohbwd b ulong t ulong sc f64 to void
v = get og 0
pr = add get og 18 mul t v
y = get oby add mul b get og 1 t
kdlog pr v y sc
ohbwd2 pr t
end

note p[c] = (p[c] - [c = y]) sc for c < n
fn kdlog po ulong n ulong y ulong sc f64 to void
for c ulong n
g = get oa add po c
if eq c y
g = sub g 1.0
end
put oa add po c mul g sc
end
end

fn ohbwd2 pr ulong t ulong to void
d = get og 2
v = get og 0
r = mul t d
z = add get og 17 r
kger pr z get og 10 v d
dz = add get og 25 r
kvm pr ulong 0 dz v d
hf = add get og 15 r
dh = add get og 19 r
brms hf get og 33 add get og 16 t dz dh
end

note Mutant lp (the w2 gradient of a layer application that repeats an earlier parameter layer is
note dropped, so a core w2 gets only the gradient of its first pass): 1 in the product, 0 in the
note mutant, which gcheck on a looped checkpoint must catch. Without a loop the two are the same.
note (Named OMUTLP: OMUTL is gpu/gk.om's BF16 mutant l, and the gb10 unit holds both files.)
const OMUTLP ulong 1

note FFN backward of row t of layer l; DH[t] holds d(out) and gains the rms2 path
fn offb l ulong t ulong to void
f = get og 4
dh = add get og 19 mul t get og 2
df = add get og 26 mul t f
ozero df f
kvta dh ovw2 l df f get og 2
if eq get ogkm 0 0
kdrelu df add oafp l mul t f f
else
ogmask df l t
end
g2 = add get og 10 ovw2 l
if or eq OMUTLP 1 eq olp l l
kger add oarl l mul t f dh g2 f get og 2
end
offb2 l t df
end

note y[j] = 0 where x[j] <= 0, for j < n
fn kdrelu yo ulong xo ulong n ulong to void
for j ulong n
if le get oa add xo j 0.0
put oa add yo j 0.0f64
end
end
end

fn offb2 l ulong t ulong df ulong to void
d = get og 2
r = mul t d
g1 = add get og 10 ovw1 l
kger add oabn l r df g1 d get og 4
da = add get og 20 r
ozero da d
kvta df ovw1 l da d get og 4
hm = add oahm l r
dh = add get og 19 r
brms hm ovg2 l add oas2 l t da dh
end

note dp[j] = dO[t].u[j] (head n) into TMP; returns sum_j p[j] dp[j]
fn oattd l ulong n ulong t ulong to f64
e = get og 7
dor = add add get og 24 mul t get og 2 mul n e
uo = add oau l mul n e
pa = opar l n t
ret kattd dor uo pa add t 1
end

fn kattd dor ulong uo ulong pa ulong nj ulong to f64
d = get og 2
de = add dor get og 7
dt = 0.0f64
j = ulong 0
while le add j 4 nj bound 999999
kdot4a dor de uo d
dt = kattd4 add pa j add get og 27 j dt
uo = add uo mul 4 d
j = add j 4
end
while lt j nj bound 4
dp = kdot1a dor de uo
put oa add get og 27 j dp
a = get opa add pa j
dt = add dt mul a dp
uo = add uo d
j = add j 1
end
ret dt
end

note TMP[tm + m] = oq[m]; dt += PA[p + m] oq[m] for m < 4 in order
fn kattd4 p ulong tm ulong dt f64 to f64
for i ulong 4
dp = get oq i
put oa add tm i dp
a = get opa add p i
dt = add dt mul a dp
end
ret dt
end

note scratch offsets of oatta: 0 q[t], 1 dq[t], 2 dO[t], 3 k, 4 dk, 5 du (head n applied)
global oz ulong 8

note ds[j] = p[j](dp[j] - dot)/sqrt(E); dq[t] += ds k[j]; dk[j] += ds q[t]; du[j] += p[j] dO[t]
fn oatta l ulong n ulong t ulong dt f64 to void
e = get og 7
hn = mul n e
r = mul t get og 2
put ofs 2 dt
put oz 0 add add oaq l r hn
put oz 1 add add get og 21 r hn
put oz 2 add add get og 24 r hn
put oz 3 add oak l hn
put oz 4 add get og 22 hn
put oz 5 add get og 23 hn
pa = opar l n t
oatta2 pa add t 1
end

fn oatta2 pa ulong nj ulong to void
d = get og 2
e = get og 7
for j ulong nj
jr = mul j d
ds = oads pa j
kaxpy get oz 1 add get oz 3 jr ds e
if eq OMUTA 1
kaxpy add get oz 4 jr get oz 0 ds e
else
kaxpy add get oz 4 jr get oz 0 neg ds e
end
pj = get opa add pa j
kaxpy add get oz 5 jr get oz 2 pj e
end
end

note ds[j] = p[j] (TMP[j] - dot) / sqrt(E), dot in ofs 2
fn oads pa ulong j ulong to f64
pj = get opa add pa j
u = sub get oa add get og 27 j get ofs 2
ret div mul pj u fsqrt f64 get og 7
end

fn olayb l ulong to void
ostw olp l
oaflip l false
ct = get og 9
for t ulong ct
offb l t
end
for t2 ulong ct
olaybo l t2
end
d = get og 2
ozero get og 21 mul ct d
ozero get og 22 mul ct d
ozero get og 23 mul ct d
for n ulong get og 3
for t3 ulong ct
dt = oattd l n t3
oatta l n t3 dt
end
end
for t4 ulong ct
olayb2 l t4
end
end

note row t: dO[t] = DH[t] . wo^T; dwo += o[t] DH[t]
fn olaybo l ulong t ulong to void
d = get og 2
r = mul t d
dor = add get og 24 r
dh = add get og 19 r
ozero dor d
kvta dh ovwo l dor d d
kger add oao l r dh add get og 10 ovwo l d d
end

note da = dq.wq^T + dk.wk^T + du.wv^T; weight gradients; DH[t] gains the rms1 path
fn olayb2 l ulong t ulong to void
d = get og 2
r = mul t d
da = add get og 20 r
ozero da d
kvta add get og 21 r ovwq l da d d
kvta add get og 22 r ovwk l da d d
kvta add get og 23 r ovwv l da d d
olayb3 l t
end

fn olayb3 l ulong t ulong to void
d = get og 2
r = mul t d
a = add oaa l r
g0 = get og 10
kger a add get og 21 r add g0 ovwq l d d
kger a add get og 22 r add g0 ovwk l d d
kger a add get og 23 r add g0 ovwv l d d
hi = add oahin l r
dh = add get og 19 r
brms hi ovg1 l add oas1 l t add get og 20 r dh
end

note backward pass of sequence b after ofwd b; sc = 1/(T B) scales dl so the gradient is that of
note the step loss. Gradients accumulate into the gradient at og[10] in ogr.
fn obwd b ulong sc f64 to void
ct = get og 9
ozero get og 19 mul ct get og 2
for t ulong ct
ohbwd b t sc
end
ll = get og 56
fl = get ofzlay 0
for i ulong sub ll fl
olayb sub sub ll 1 i
end
if eq fl 0
for t2 ulong ct
obwde b t2
end
end
end

note row t: dwte[x[t]] += DH[t]; dwpe[t] += DH[t]
fn obwde b ulong t ulong to void
d = get og 2
c = get obx add mul b get og 1 t
dh = add get og 19 mul t d
g0 = get og 10
kaxpg add g0 mul c d dh 1.0 d
kaxpg add add g0 get og 30 mul t d dh 1.0 d
end
